/P 148 0 R
/T (    Long ago, in a divided realm of what is now known as the Republic of the Philippines, there stood numerous great kingdoms, ruled by Rajas, Datus, and Sultans. Located in the very heart of these lands was the Kingdom of Marilag.)
/E (    Long ago, in a divided realm of what is now known as the Republic of the Philippines, there stood numerous great kingdoms, ruled by Rajas, Datus, and Sultans. Located in the very heart of these lands was the Kingdom of Marilag.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
203 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 148 0 R
/T (    The sea had always been kind to Marilag. It brought merchants to its shores, filled fishermen's nets with fish, and carried balangays toward distant lands. For hundreds of years, the people had lived by its blessings, believing that tomorrow would bring another good harvest and another peaceful day.)
/E (    The sea had always been kind to Marilag. It brought merchants to its shores, filled fishermen's nets with fish, and carried balangays toward distant lands. For hundreds of years, the people had lived by its blessings, believing that tomorrow would bring another good harvest and another peaceful day.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [1]
>>
