/T (      For weeks, Marilag resisted. The Akbari forces expected a kingdom without its Raja to be easy to control. Instead, every village became another place where their authority was challenged. Eventually, the Akbari soldiers were forced to retreat toward the coast. Their supplies had begun to run low, and the people they had expected to control refused to cooperate with them.)
